    "result_text": "All tests pass (exit code 0). The audit output confirms the change is working correctly:\n\n- **V2 member id**: `NSWV22716E6609E7` \u2014 the region code inside the identifier now carries the `V2` tag (`NSWV2\u2026` instead of `NSW\u2026`).\n- **Audit event schema v2**: `{\"seq\":1,...,\"ownerSegment\":\"STANDARD_METRO\",\"membershipLevel\":1,\"schemaVersion\":2,\"event\":\"OWNER_CREATED\"}` \u2014 `schemaVersion: 2` added and `ownerSegment` recomputed from the V2 owner.\n- **Owner segment `STANDARD_METRO`** \u2014 `METRO` proves the segment's derived region is still the plain `NSW` locality (not `NSWV2`), so the V2 tag did not leak into locality/timezone/segment.\n\n## Summary of changes\n\n**`Owner.java`** \u2014 Added `IDENTITY_VERSION_TAG = \"V2\"` and changed `getIdentityRegionCode()` to return `getRegion() + \"V2\"` (the region stamped inside identifiers). `getLocality()`, `getTimezone()` and `getOwnerSegment()` are untouched, so they keep the plain region code.\n\n**`OwnerRestControllerV1.java`** \u2014 Mixed the `V2` tag into the hash material of both `identityKey()` (`\"V2|tel|email|soundex\"`) and `householdId()` (`\"V2|lastName|postcode\"`). `memberId` picks up V2 automatically via `getIdentityRegionCode()`. Javadocs updated.\n\n**`openapi.yml`** \u2014 Removed top-level `memberId`/`householdId`/`identityKey` from `Owner`; added a top-level `apiVersion` (int) and an `identity` object referencing a new `OwnerIdentity` schema (holding the three identifiers). Updated the `locality` description to reflect it stays the plain region.\n\n**`OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 Maps `apiVersion` to the constant `2` and builds the nested `identity` object from the owner's derived identifiers.\n\n**`OwnerCreatedEvent.java`** \u2014 Record now emits `{seq, ownerId, memberId, ownerSegment, membershipLevel, schemaVersion, event}` with `schemaVersion = 2` and the owner segment recomputed from the V2 owner.\n\nThe request fields are unchanged, and the full suite is green.",
