    "probe_text": "Here is the complete, ordered sequence for `POST /api/owners`, from the framework layer through `addOwner` \u2192 `createOwner` and back. Validations (V) reject the request; side-effects (S) mutate state or the outside world.\n\n## Before the controller body runs (framework)\n\n1. **V \u2014 Authorization.** `@PreAuthorize(\"hasRole(@roles.OWNER_ADMIN)\")` on `addOwner`; caller must hold the `OWNER_ADMIN` role.\n2. **V \u2014 Bean Validation** on the `@Valid @RequestBody OwnerFieldsDto` (all fail with `400`):\n   - `title` \u2014 `@Size(max 10)`\n   - `firstName` \u2014 `@NotNull`, `@Pattern` (letters, up to 3 space/`'`/`-`-joined words), `@Size(1..30)`\n   - `lastName` \u2014 `@NotNull`, `@Pattern` (same, optional trailing `.`), `@Size(1..30)`\n   - `address` \u2014 when present, `@Pattern` (non-blank), `@Size(1..255)`\n   - `addressLine1` \u2014 when present, `@Pattern` (non-blank), `@Size(1..255)`\n   - `addressLine2` \u2014 `@Size(max 255)`\n   - `city` \u2014 `@NotNull`, `@Pattern` (non-blank), `@Size(1..80)`\n   - `postcode` \u2014 when present, `@Pattern(^[0-9]{4}$)`\n   - `telephone` \u2014 `@NotNull`, `@Size(1..20)`\n   - `email` \u2014 when present, `@Size(max 255)`, `@Email`\n\n## `addOwner` entry point\n\n3. **S / short-circuit \u2014 Idempotency replay.** Reads the non-blank `Idempotency-Key` header; if that key was already recorded for a still-existing owner, returns that owner with `200 OK` and **no create occurs** (rest of the pipeline is skipped).\n\n## `createOwner` pipeline (only if not replayed)\n\n4. **S \u2014 Map DTO \u2192 `Owner`** via `ownerMapper.toOwner`.\n5. **V/S \u2014 `normalizeAndValidateFields`** (any failure \u2192 `400`), in this sub-order:\n   1. **Address** (`normalizeAddressFields`): if `addressLine1` is non-blank, normalize line1/line2 (trim, collapse inner whitespace, upper-case, expand `ST\u2192STREET`, `RD\u2192ROAD`, `AVE\u2192AVENUE`), write them back and **compose the flat `address`**; otherwise normalize the flat `address`. Reject if no non-blank address results. *(side-effect: rewrites address fields)*\n   2. **Email** (if supplied): trim + lower-case; must match the email regex; reject if the domain is a disposable domain (`mailinator.com`, `tempmail.com`, `guerrillamail.com`); else **store normalized email**.\n   3. **Postcode** (`isPostcodeValidForCity`): null allowed; else must be 4 digits and, if the city maps to a known region, fall inside that region's range (NSW 2000\u20132099, VIC 3000\u20133099, QLD 4000\u20134099).\n   4. **Telephone** (`normalizeTelephone`): strip spaces/dashes/brackets; keep `+`/country code or assume `+61` and drop one leading `0`; must be E.164 (`+` then 8\u201315 digits) with the correct national-number length for its country code; reject if not; else **store normalized telephone**.\n6. **V \u2014 Future registration date.** If a `registrationDate` was supplied and is after today \u2192 `400`.\n7. **S \u2014 Resolve & set registration date** (`resolveRegistrationDate`): supplied date or today, rolled forward to the next business day (skipping weekends and the fixed 2026 public-holiday list); assigned onto the owner.\n8. **V \u2014 Daily cap.** If \u2265 100 existing owners already carry that resolved registration date \u2192 `429 TOO_MANY_REQUESTS`.\n9. **S \u2014 Set `householdId`** (`householdId(owner)`).\n10. **S \u2014 Set `identityKey`** (`identityKey(owner)`).\n11. **V \u2014 Hard duplicate.** If the `identityKey` matches any non-deleted existing owner \u2192 `409 CONFLICT`.\n12. Read the `sharesHousehold` flag from the request.\n13. **V \u2014 Per-city hard capacity.** If the owner's city already holds \u2265 50 owners \u2192 `409 CONFLICT`.\n14. **S \u2014 `assignRegistrationAttributes`** (derived fields, computed before save while counts still exclude this owner):\n    - `memberId` (`generateMemberId`, including de-duplication against existing member ids by appending `-<n>`)\n    - `householdId` (recomputed)\n    - `namesakeCount`\n    - `householdMemberCount`\n    - `membershipLevelCap`\n    - possible-duplicate flags: if `sharesHousehold` is true \u2192 `possibleDuplicate=false`, `possibleDuplicateOf=null`; otherwise `assignPossibleDuplicate` sets them from a soft (postcode + last-name Soundex, different identity key) match.\n15. **S \u2014 Persist** via `clinicService.saveOwner(owner)` (assigns the id).\n16. **S \u2014 Audit.** `auditOwnerCreated`: two `AUDIT` log lines \u2014 a human-readable line and a structured `OwnerCreatedEvent` JSON with an incremented sequence number.\n17. **S \u2014 Notify.** `enqueueWelcomeNotification`: one `NOTIFY` welcome log line.\n18. **S \u2014 Build `Location` header** `/api/owners/{id}`.\n19. **S \u2014 Build response DTO** (`buildOwnerDto`): attaches the read-time derived flags `bulkSignupWarning`, `capacityWarning`, `riskFlag`.\n\n## Back in `addOwner`\n\n20. **S \u2014 Record idempotency.** If an `Idempotency-Key` was present and the result is `201` with an id, store `key \u2192 id` in the `idempotentCreates` map.\n21. Return **`201 CREATED`** with the owner and `Location` header.\n\nA note on ordering: field normalization/validation (step 5) runs *before* the future-date check (6) and before the daily-cap, duplicate, and capacity gates. The gate order is **400 (fields/future date) \u2192 429 (daily cap) \u2192 409 (identity duplicate) \u2192 409 (city capacity)**, and all the derived-attribute side-effects happen only after every gate has passed."
